## Copy-paste — user prompt preamble (repeat in chat when scoping assessments)

Produce **two labeled scores**:

- **`(A) V1.1 headline readiness (100)`** — only in-contract V1 / V1.1 gates per `docs/library/V1_SCOPE.md`, `docs/library/V1_DEFERRED.md`, and trust-center commitments. **Out of `(A)`:** SOC 2 CPA attestation, ISO certificate, signed design partner, **public third-party extension/plugin SDK**, **MCP absence in V1** (MCP is **V1.1**-scoped per docs), **third-party plugin marketplace / agent store**, and **participant user testing with assistive technologies** (not a projected ICP commitment in headline scoring) — cite under **`(B)`** or roadmap only when relevant.
- **`(B) Procurement / market-motion realism (informational, not weighted into `(A)`)`** — buyer friction incl. SOC 2 report expectations; optional GTM pipeline (design partner, reference pipeline) **only if the user asked**.

Do **not** reduce **`(A)`** for missing CPA SOC 2 / ISO certs, lacking a design partner, lacking a public extension SDK, lacking MCP in V1, lacking a third-party plugin marketplace, **not having run user tests with assistive technologies**, or **absence of sales-engineer-led LLM setup on ArchLucid-hosted SaaS**; summarize interim posture + roadmap citations instead.
